Package: uzunyx-altguard
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: emi <285864120+antarest47@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: kwin-wayland (>= @KWIN@), kwin-wayland (<< @KWIN@.~)
Description: keeps apps from opening their menu after an Alt shortcut
 KWin plugin. Apps such as Firefox, Electron apps or LibreOffice open their
 menu when Alt is pressed and released alone. When Alt is used with a global
 shortcut (Alt+W, Alt+1…) or to move a window with the mouse, KWin keeps the
 other key and the app only sees Alt, so the menu opens. This plugin sends
 the focused window a harmless F24 key just before Alt is released, so the
 app knows Alt was not alone. Alt alone and Alt+letter inside apps work as
 before.
 .
 Built against one exact KWin version: KWin refuses to load it in any
 other, so it must be rebuilt after every KWin update.
